  m_text: 'It''s the beginning portion of the largest blood vessel in your body.
    It carries oxygen-rich blood from your heart to the rest of your aorta. Your
    two main coronary arteries branch off of the ascending aorta. At its root, it
    contains two aortic sinuses: Right and Left aortic sinus. They supply the myocardium
    of the heart'
